From e4f60e70f081eb1f17f381eeff5491ee308bb8fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <noduhgamingxd@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:51:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] staging: media: tegra-video: support the grate host1x

The libre-tegra tree has two mutually exclusive host1x implementations:
the mainline one (TEGRA_HOST1X) and the grate one (GRATE_HOST1X). The
Tegra video driver only built against the former, so it could not be
enabled in a kernel using the grate stack.

Add host1x-compat.h, which selects the right header and provides the
few sync point helpers the VI code needs on top of whichever API is in
use. The grate host1x can allocate, read and release a sync point but
has no request-with-flags, id or wait-on-threshold calls, so there the
wait polls the hardware counter. The grate host1x_driver remove callback
returns int rather than void.

Allow VIDEO_TEGRA with either host1x. Behaviour with the mainline host1x
is unchanged.
